            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0696" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163 Property/25</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November 8,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 27.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1740</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to the Legation’s radio message
                    No. 591, of August 2, 10 a.m., concerning the regulations governing the lease of
                    land and buildings in the interior by foreign missionary societies, I have the
                    honor to enclose copy, in translation, of a despatch from the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs of the Nationalist Government.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that, in this despatch, Dr. Wang confines himself to rather
                    vague assurances that the regulations will not adversely affect American
                    missionary interests, and that, consequently, the Legation need have no
                    apprehensions.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. V. A.
                    MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d578-a1.xml" xpointer="d578-a1"/>
            </div>
